From 6ff98056dddf1035d864a950f9e2639a2957c4ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 21:53:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] CI: fix the workflow parse error, the wasm call site and
 clippy lints

- .github/workflows/csl-proving.yml: quote a step name that contained
  ": " (the YAML parser rejected the file, so the real-proving job never
  started); build the coin-structure unit test in release like the other
  steps so the job compiles one profile.
- ledger-wasm/src/zswap_wasm.rs: pass the `derivation` argument (`None`)
  to `Input::new_contract_owned`. The signature gained it in the first
  experiment commit and the wasm build had been failing since.
- zkir/src/csl_whitelist.rs, ledger/tests/csl_*.rs: satisfy clippy under
  the upstream `-D warnings` flags (manual_is_multiple_of,
  useless_conversion, err_expect, needless_late_init). No behavioural
  change; `cargo clippy --all-targets --workspace --all-features` with the
  upstream allow-list passes on rustc 1.97.0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Q9CJgdhDhwqKR5eCeFM2VG
